.TH SUBSYSTEM_DEBUG 4 2026-10-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
subsystem_debug \- global mask of Lustre subsystems that may log debug messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.B lctl get_param subsystem_debug
.SY
.B lctl set_param subsystem_debug=
.RI { SUBSYSTEM_LIST | HEX_MASK }
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Global
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB subsystem_debug= -1
.RB "(all subsystems)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B subsystem_debug
parameter filters non-mandatory message classes by code subsystem.
A
.BR CDEBUG ()
call with a non-mandatory class is only kept if its subsystem is set in
.B subsystem_debug
.I and
its class is set in the applicable mask, from
.BR debug (4)
or an override in
.BR debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM (4).
The mandatory classes
.BR error ,
.BR warning ,
.B emerg
and
.B console
are logged regardless of subsystem selection.
.PP
.I SUBSYSTEM_LIST
is a comma, space, or plus-separated list of subsystem names, or a
.I HEX_MASK
(hexadecimal or decimal number).
The value
.B -1
(or
.BR all )
enables every subsystem;
.B 0
disables non-mandatory messages from all subsystems.
.PP
The following subsystems are defined:
.TP
.B undefined
Code that logs with
.BR CDEBUG ()
but has not set
.BR DEBUG_SUBSYSTEM .
Selected by default (bit 0), but has no
.B debug_subsystem.undefined
override file, so its messages always follow the global
.BR debug (4)
mask.
.TP
.B mdc
Metadata client.
.TP
.B mds
Metadata server.
.TP
.B osc
Object storage client.
.TP
.B ost
Object storage target (server side of OST).
.TP
.B class
The obd_class device/layering framework shared by all Lustre modules.
.TP
.B log
Llog (on-disk and in-memory configuration/changelog) record handling.
.TP
.B llite
Lustre client filesystem (VFS-facing) code.
.TP
.B rpc
PtlRPC request/reply handling that is not specific to one subsystem.
.TP
.B mgmt
Currently has no code setting
.B DEBUG_SUBSYSTEM
to this value.
.TP
.B lnet
Lustre Networking core.
.TP
.B lnd
LNet Network Drivers (all transports).
.TP
.B pinger
Currently has no code setting
.B DEBUG_SUBSYSTEM
to this value; the client pinger logs under
.B rpc
instead.
.TP
.B filter
OST object storage (OFD).
.TP
.B libcfs
Currently has no code setting
.B DEBUG_SUBSYSTEM
to this value; the libcfs portability layer logs under
.B lnet
instead.
.TP
.B echo
The echo client and server test modules.
.TP
.B ldlm
The Distributed Lock Manager.
.TP
.B lov
Logical Object Volume (client-side striping).
.TP
.B lquota
Lustre quota accounting and enforcement.
.TP
.B osd
Object Storage Device backend (ldiskfs or ZFS).
.TP
.B lfsck
Distributed filesystem consistency check and repair.
.TP
.B snapshot
Filesystem snapshot creation and management.
.TP
.B lmv
Logical Metadata Volume (client-side directory striping).
.TP
.B sec
PtlRPC security (sptlrpc, GSS/Kerberos, SSK) and identity upcall cache.
.TP
.B gss
Currently has no code setting
.B DEBUG_SUBSYSTEM
to this value; GSS/Kerberos code logs under
.B sec
instead.
.TP
.B mgc
Management client.
.TP
.B mgs
Management server.
.TP
.B fid
File identifier (FID) allocation and sequence management.
.TP
.B fld
FID location database (maps FID sequences to MDTs).
.PP
Since release 2.18.0, a subsystem's contribution to
.B debug
can be overridden independently with
.BR debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM (4),
without changing
.B subsystem_debug
or the global
.B debug
mask.
.SH EXAMPLES
Log only LDLM and LLITE subsystems:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param subsystem_debug=ldlm+llite"
.EE
.PP
Restore the default (all subsystems):
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param subsystem_debug=-1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B subsystem_debug
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 0.7.0,
.\" commit 0.7.0-0-g96ec6856f9
but per-subsystem overrides of the
.BR debug (4)
mask with
.BR debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM (4)
are only available since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.6x
.SH SEE ALSO
